Verona development ledger
Newest entries first. Perpetual history; excluded from finite issue inventory.

2026-11-18 - Real local speaking-face window qualified
Action: Added Verona.cmd, bounded loopback capability API and dependency-free
WebGL2/audio player. Reused installed voices and CPU model; no new package.
Mechanism: Authenticated binary buffers, aligned Uint32 topology, GPU frame
interpolation from audio.currentTime, one in-RAM clip and explicit retryable
errors. No separate face clock, autoplay, file server or cloud inference.
Evidence: Twenty-five focused checks; twelve actual Edge/browser-v3 scenarios
pass, including all three voices, four expression inputs, P/B/M/F/V/vowels,
transport, overlong-speech rejection, injected failure/retry and reload.
Inspected actual screenshots. Zero page exceptions/external page requests;
owned server/browser stopped and disposable test profile removed.
Corrections: v1 harness clicks lacked trusted audio activation; used actual
pointer events rather than bypassing autoplay. v2 final diagnostic assumed
nonempty Edge errorText; asserted observed inspector blockedReason in v3.
Meaning: Functional neural-skin prototype exists; muted checks are not listening
acceptance or an anatomical-contact benchmark. Full SDK postprocessing and
independent teeth/tongue/eye joints remain omitted. Chapter06 explains boundaries.
Definition: Reconciled text-first product brief and closed finite vr-03 scope.
Next consequence: Publish this coherent player slice and seal owned continuity/
tracking; no active service is left running for the sleeping owner.

2026-11-18 - Complete local text-to-face clip, before the graphical player
Action: Reused installed Windows System.Speech and the pinned Mark CPU network;
fetched one official hash-verified matching Maya-ACE Mark topology data file.
Mechanism: Fixed PowerShell program plus JSON stdin, bounded speech/threads,
non-executing numerical Maya parser, native-edge-constrained mesh clustering
and complete rational-time neural skin clips. No new Python/TTS stack.
Evidence: "Hey, how are you?" generates2.745s/83frames/10,349vertices/5.15MBmotion;
1.894s motion work excluding synthesis/startup, median20.47ms network frame.
Nineteen focused checks and dependency consistency pass. Chapter06 is canonical.
Actual corrections: Maya omits the polygon type after its first chunk; parsing
only typed chunks lost faces. Corrected and tested continuation/signed edges.
The first new test also had an invalid grouped context-manager fixture; fixed
before the successful full check. No failed run is counted as passing.
Tracking: vr-07 issue6 and original item verified In Progress after ordinary
new-membership propagation lag; saved IDs reused, never recreated.
Next consequence: Implement visible playback and real browser checks. Skin
postprocess, independent teeth/tongue/eyes and human accuracy remain unqualified.

